    <innernamespace refid="namespaceanonymous__namespace_02passwordworker_8cpp_03">anonymous_namespace{passwordworker.cpp}</innernamespace>
    <briefdescription>
<para>Builds the password thread pool using settings from the <ref refid="classConfigurator" kindref="compound">Configurator</ref>. (Originally: &quot;Implementation for passwordworker: Fetches the
password-worker sizing from the globally configured Configurator.&quot;). </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This file reads how many worker threads and how large a queue to create, then passes those numbers to the BoundedExecutor base class. It contains only two constructors, no logic of its own.</para>
<para>WHY THIS FILE MATTERS IN THE SERVER: It connects the password worker pool to the server&apos;s runtime configuration, so administrators can tune how much password work the server will do at once without changing code. Without it, the pool sizes would be hard-coded.</para>
<para>CONCEPTS TO LEARN (for beginners):<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Constructor initializer lists: <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/initializer_list">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/initializer_list</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>The singleton/service-locator pattern: <ulink url="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Service_locator_pattern">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Service_locator_pattern</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Configuration objects: <ulink url="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Configuration_file">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Configuration_file</ulink></para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><simplesect kind="author"><para>Amr Osman <ulink url="mailto:dr3mro@gmail.com">dr3mro@gmail.com</ulink> </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="date"><para>2026-11-16 </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
